# NCCN Breast Cancer 2025 Guidelines <span class="tag" tag-name="Reference"><span class="smallcaps">Reference</span></span>

## Systemic therapies (neoadjuvant and adjuvant) for EBC

### Preoperative therapy

- **Role of neoadjuvant therapy in breast cancer** - historical RCTs demonstrated no statistically significant differences when <u>systemic chemotherapy</u> employed in the pre-operative and post-operative stages: 
![](~/Documents/notes/img/principles_of_preoperative_systemic_therapy_in_operable_breast_cancer_1.png)
- **Options for preoperative therapy:**
  - <u>Chemotherapy</u> - chemotherapy regimens applicable to the adjuvant setting can be applied in the pre-operative setting for eradication or control of undiscovered micrometastasis
  - <u>Endocrine therapy</u> - aromatase inhibitor (w/ OFS in premenopausal women), or tamoxifen for HR+ tumours
  - <u>HER2-targeted therapy</u> - Pertuzumab, trastuzumab and docetaxel for patients w/ HER+ EBC
  - <u>Immunotherapy</u> - role of chemoimmunotherapy (w/ pembrolizumab) in the pre-operative setting for operable TNBC
- **Response assessment during pre-operative chemotherapy** - NCCN recommendations:
  - <u>Modality</u>:
    - By regular clinical exam
    - Routine mammography not performed regularly but may be considered if tumor progression is suspected
  - <u>Role</u>:
    - **Detection of disease progression** - Disease progression while undergoing preoperative systemic therapy should be taken promptly to surgery
    - **Prognostic** - residual cancer burden (RCB) after pre-operative chemotherapy appears to be a poor prognostic marker irrespective of histological subtype (HR 1.55-2.16 for worse EFS across different cancer subtypes)
- **Indications for pre-operative therapy:**
  - **Absolute indications for pre-operative systemic therapy:**
    - <u>Inoperable breast cancer</u> - e.g. inflammatory breast cancer, bulky or matted cN2 disease, cN3 disease, cT4 tumours
    - <u>Operable breast cancer</u> - by principle reserved for those 1) wishing for breast conservation, 2) a/w poor prognostic disease, or 3) predicted good response to systemic therapy:
      - Large primary tumours relative to breast size in a patient who wish for breast conservation
      - HER2+ EBC or TNBC (esp. if \>= cT2, or \>= cN1, but can be considered for cT1N0 disease)
      - HR w/ high-likelihood of response based on 21 gene assay recurrence score for postmenopausal women
  - **Absolute contraindications for pre-operative systemic therapy:**
    - Extensive DCIS when extent of invasive carcinoma not well-defined
    - Patients with poorly delineated extent of disease
    - Non-palpable tumours that are not clinically assessable
- **Approach to pre-operative systemic therapy selection:**
  - <u>Whether pre-operative systemic therapy benefits the patient</u> - see above for absolute indications and contraindications
  - <u>Molecular subtyupes of breast cancer</u> - therapy dependent on HR+, HER2+ or TNBC

### Adjuvant systemic therapy

- **Dependent on:**

  - 1\. Utilisation of neoadjuvant therapy
  - 2\. Histology
  - 3\. HR status and HER2 expression
  - 4\. Risk of recurrence

- **Stratification for systemic adjuvant therapy:**

  - <u>Stratification by histology</u> - rare favourable subtypes have additional considerations
  - <u>Stratification of HR-status and HER2 expression</u>:
    - HR+ disease - by definition ER+/HR+ and HER2-
    - HER2+ disease - by definition HER2+ irrespective of HR-status (however response to targeted therapy may be related to HR status)
    - TNBC - by definition HR- and HER2-
  - <u>Stratification by hormonal status and risk features</u> - role in HR+ HER2- (luminal) disease to determine the intensity of hormonal therapy and chemotherapy

  
  ![](~/Documents/notes/img/approach_to_systemic_therapy_for_adjuvant_therapy_after_upfront_surgery.png)

- **Definition of HR positivity:**

  - <u>ER positivitity</u> - 1%-100% tumour cells stianing positive for ER in IHC considered ER+ and are elligible for endocrine therapy (however ER-low+ \[1-10%\] have been reported to be more heterogenous in biology and behave more like ER- disease)
  - <u>HR positivity</u> - 1%-100 of cells staining positive for PR in IHC

- **Adjuvant systemic therapy for HR+, HER2- tumours** - Endocrine therapy +/- chemotherapy (if high risk of recurrence):

  - **Endocrine therapy:**
    - **Tamoxifen** (SERMs):
      - <u>Indications</u> - for both pre- and post-menopausal women
      - <u>Duration</u> - 5y of tamoxifen or extended therapy (10y) for selected patients
      - <u>Evidence</u>:
        - ATLAS trial demonstrated significant reduction in recurrence and death from breast cancer with 10y versus 5y of tamoxifen
      - <u>S/E</u> - most important S/E include:
        - Increased risk of **endometrial carcinoma**
        - Increased risk of DVT and P/E
    - **Aromatase inhibitors** - AIs are only active in those w/o functional ovaries:
